equired.\nGraduate Admission\nGraduate Admission\nPrevious\nNext\nRIT/\nAdmissions and Aid/\nGraduate Admission\nInvest in a degree with real-world return.\nOur graduate programs are built at the intersection of technology, art, and design\u2014preparing you for what's next. Explore our career outcomes, research achievements, and alumni success stories.\nSee the impact of an RIT graduate degree\n$91.9K\nAverage Reported First-Year Salary\nThe average reported salary for students with an RIT master\u2019s degree in their first post-graduate year\n#5\nAmong Top Schools\u2019 Co-op or Internship Programs\nU.S. News & World Report 2027\n#95\nNational Universities\nRanked among the top 100 of national universities\nTop 1K\nBest Global Universities\nAwarded for quality research and global reputation\n#5\nTop School for Co-op or Internship Programs\nRanked among nation\u2019s best in hands-on career preparation\nJump to Section\nEvents and Webinars\nGraduate Programs\nHow to Apply\nFinancial Aid and Scholarships\nConnect with a Student\nAccepted Students\nContact Us\nEvents and Webinars\nDiscover how graduate study at RIT can help further your career objectives.\nVirtual Admissions Webinars | Recordings available\nVirtual Academic Sessions | October 20 - October 29\nOn-Campus Open House | November 20\nLearn more and register\nDon't Delay Your Ambitions Until the Fall\nRIT offers 45+ programs that you can begin in spring. Jumpstart your graduate journey and begin your studies this January.\nLearn how to apply\nUpcoming Webinars\nGet in-depth information about degrees, how to apply, and how to fund your education through our webinar series.\nRegister for a webinar\nPrevious\nNext\nView all upcoming events\n100+ Future-Focused Graduate Programs\nMaster\u2019s Degrees\nDoctoral Degrees\nAdvanced Certificates\nOnline Degrees\nYou can also check out past event recordings and browse our informational events.\nReady to apply?\nTake the next step toward transforming your passion into purpose\u2014explore our step-by-step application process and get ready to join the RIT community.\nLearn how to apply\nFinancial Aid and Scholarships\nAssistantships, loans, scholarships, co-op wages, and multiple other sources can help fund your graduate education.\nThe cost of an RIT graduate degree varies. The number of credits taken per semester, delivery method (online vs on-campus), and each student\u2019s financial situation also varies. The only way to know your cost, and any aid you may qualify for, is to complete your application and receive a decision.\nEstimate Your Graduate Tuition Sources of Funding\nLoading...\nConnect with a Student\nConnect with a current student to hear about their RIT experience and ask your questions.\nLearn more\nAccepted Students\nYou\u2019re in. What\u2019s next?\nCongratulations on your admission to RIT! Explore your next steps, lock in your spot, and get ready to join RIT's graduate community.\nLearn more\nContact Admissions\nEach degree program is assigned an admissions counselor to help you choose the right program, navigate requirements, and answer your questions.\nEnter your degree to find your counselor.\nContact\nLive chat with admissions\nSchedule a campus visit\nAttend a webinar\nEmail us\nStay Connected\nMailing Address\nGraduate Admissions\nBausch and Lomb Center\n58 Lomb Memorial Drive\nRochester Institute of Technology\nRochester, New York 14623-5604\nGetting to Admissions and Aid\ngradinfo@rit.edu\nPhone: 585-475-2229\nFax: 585-475-7164\nFrequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\nAddress and Phone\nContact Us\nAdmissions and Aid Overview\nFirst-Year Admission\nTransfer Admission\nGraduate Admission\nInternational Students\nDeaf and Hard-of-Hearing Students\nUS Military / Veterans\nOnline Education Admission\nFinancial Aid and Scholarships\nTuition and Fees\nVisit RIT\nMeet us on campus\nApply for Fall 2027\nAddress and Phone\n1 Lomb Memorial Drive\nRochester, NY 14623\n585-475-2411\nWebsite feedback\nSign up for RIT